Cross-check an ext2/3/4 image superblock, group descriptors and allocation bitmaps (e2fsck-class), read-only

Usage: android-doctor fsck [OPTIONS] <IMAGE>

Arguments:
  <IMAGE>  An ext2/3/4 image

Options:
      --json                      Print the doctor/1 JSON envelope instead of text
      --baseline <BASELINE>       Only report findings whose fingerprint is not in BASELINE (a prior --json envelope, its `findings` array, or a JSON array of strings). Exit code 3 if any are new
      --baseline-mode <MODE>      How a baseline finding is matched [default: fingerprint] [possible values: fingerprint, subject, message, id]
      --baseline-file <FILE>      Re-read BASELINE from FILE on every comparison (human mode: for live comparison)
      --sarif <FILE>              Also write the findings as SARIF 2.1.0 to FILE
      --sarif-suppressions        Add suppression entries for baselined findings (only with --sarif and --baseline)
      --exclude <RULE>            Ignore findings whose rule id matches RULE (repeatable)
      --fail-on <SEVERITY>        Exit 1 on a finding at or above this severity; audit gates on medium by default, diff on high [possible values: critical, high, medium, low, info]
      --verbose                   Print the per-image detail; without this, only summary and findings
      --no-color                  Never emit colour, even on a terminal (also honours the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -h, --help                      Print help
